     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum per dose of 850\u20131,000 mg. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nWas one of these intended?\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 1,700 mg/day total, and it may be what the 1700 figure was meant to be.\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Another dose.** Tell me the dose and frequency you want.\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note recording that you verified the dose."
      }
     ],
